      "internal": false,
      "mergeID": "68bb009096015591be86fca4",
      "mergedPostDetails": "There is a specific way that disallow you to grab your stream camera with your hand, if you put the controller right in the middle of the camera and try to grab it, you will pick up only the -view point- and not the camera, and when you release it, it goes back to its origin.\n\nProof: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VVu_rYZ1A9w\n\nIn the video you can see how you can fix it, by turning off the stream camera, turning on the photo camera, then going back to the stream camera, voilá it is fixed, no more picking up ghost camera.\n\nAs an extra bug that i caught, at the end of the video you can see me moving my hand close to the camera and pointing straight to the camera, it shows the tooltip \"Use\" like if there was something right in the middle of the camera that you can't *pick up anymore* or interact with it. So this canny is for 2 bugs.\n\nI am using Valve Index and Index controllers- been for 6 years, please bsb2e come asap to me.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1696] Can't correctly grab stream camera",
