  "details": "STR:\n\n1. Open VRC in VR\n\n2. Pull out your camera\n\n3. Get your hand near the middle of the camera's screen - you should feel the vibration that the object-to-be-grabbed changed, and see the \"Use\" tooltip - and grab the lens\n\n4. Pull it away, and see the image on your camera change as if you were grabbing the lens normally\n\n5. Open your hand and see the lens snap back to *reality, ope, there goes gravity*... i mean, back to the camera.\n\nI've checked it a couple of times, and it seems to fix itself when you change instance (after you pull out the camera on the previous one) and sometimes(?) when you set the anchor to local/world (so you can grab it *legally*) and back.\n\nAdditionally, when you turn on one of the focus modes and start pointing on the screen to choose the focus, sometimes your 'laser' pointer will be interrupted near the center by a collision with the invisible lens (probably).",
